29
00:55:49.754 --> 00:55:53.754
Thank you very much Bert. Really great. Thanks.

30
00:56:19.754 --> 00:56:23.754
Hallelujah.

31
00:56:49.754 --> 00:56:52.754
People are welcome to come and sit here still.

32
00:56:52.754 --> 00:56:54.754
We still have spots available.

33
00:56:54.754 --> 00:56:58.754
I think here still, next to Philippe and next to Fonja and Martijn.

34
00:56:58.754 --> 00:57:01.754
I see still two, two, one, two.

35
00:57:01.754 --> 00:57:06.754
But those are fine like that? Fine. Absolutely good. Absolutely good.

36
00:57:06.754 --> 00:57:09.754
Hallelujah. Everyone happy?

37
00:57:09.754 --> 00:57:12.754
What a wonderful worship.

38
00:57:13.754 --> 00:57:18.754
Today we will finish the letter to the Philippians.

39
00:57:18.754 --> 00:57:23.754
Last week we all had that building update together.

40
00:57:23.754 --> 00:57:26.754
That was really thorough and good.

41
00:57:26.754 --> 00:57:29.754
I have to be honest about it.

42
00:57:29.754 --> 00:57:34.754
Then it's halfway there and it's just better to conclude together in prayer.

43
00:57:34.754 --> 00:57:38.754
But I really want to finish that letter to the Philippians.

44
00:57:38.754 --> 00:57:41.754
Chapter 4 is a wonderful chapter.

45
00:57:41.754 --> 00:57:44.754
And I want to go through it together with us.

46
00:57:44.754 --> 00:57:48.754
Because there are two very important lessons in it.

47
00:57:48.754 --> 00:57:55.754
One lesson that I thought last week with raised eyebrows, wow.

48
00:57:55.754 --> 00:57:58.754
I had something new for myself again.

49
00:57:58.754 --> 00:58:02.754
That's great. A revelation is not something you invent that no one has ever heard before.

50
00:58:02.754 --> 00:58:05.754
That is not a revelation.

51
00:58:05.754 --> 00:58:10.754
A revelation is seeing something for yourself that you have never seen before.

52
00:58:10.754 --> 00:58:12.754
And that is a wow moment.

53
00:58:12.754 --> 00:58:18.754
And I wish for everyone in this room that we receive many, many, many revelations.

54
00:58:18.754 --> 00:58:21.754
Receiving revelations builds your life.

55
00:58:21.754 --> 00:58:27.754
If you are dry of revelations, then you really need to knock on God's door.

56
00:58:27.754 --> 00:58:30.754
Because revelations are like wells of water.

57
00:58:30.754 --> 00:58:32.754
You go from well to well.

58
00:58:32.754 --> 00:58:34.754
You go from revelation to revelation.

59
00:58:34.754 --> 00:58:39.754
You should not seek material blessings in this life, material blessings.

60
00:58:39.754 --> 00:58:41.754
That is not the goal of this life.

61
00:58:41.754 --> 00:58:44.754
The purpose of this life is to go from revelation to revelation.

62
00:58:44.754 --> 00:58:46.754
From God's Word to God's Word.

63
00:58:46.754 --> 00:58:48.754
From wow to wow.

64
00:58:48.754 --> 00:58:49.754
From hallelujah to hallelujah.

65
00:58:49.754 --> 00:58:55.754
From amen to amen.

66
00:58:55.754 --> 00:58:59.754
If I am a little vague on stage.

67
00:59:00.754 --> 00:59:01.754
Unbelievable.

68
00:59:01.754 --> 00:59:04.754
This sermon has actually been ready for two weeks.

69
00:59:04.754 --> 00:59:10.754
So this week I didn't have to do much more than just meditate on what was already there.

70
00:59:10.754 --> 00:59:12.754
And that worked out just fine.

71
00:59:12.754 --> 00:59:16.754
Because last week I started having jaw pain and toothache here.

72
00:59:16.754 --> 00:59:19.754
And it hurt so much, church.

73
00:59:19.754 --> 00:59:21.754
I was hitting the ceiling.

74
00:59:21.754 --> 00:59:23.754
Has anyone ever had a toothache?

75
00:59:23.754 --> 00:59:25.754
Boy, you can miss that like a toothache.

76
00:59:25.754 --> 00:59:27.754
That's not normal.

77
00:59:27.754 --> 00:59:30.754
That hurt, boy.

78
00:59:30.754 --> 00:59:31.754
Really not normal.

79
00:59:31.754 --> 00:59:35.754
So then you just don't know what to do with yourself.

80
00:59:35.754 --> 00:59:37.754
I once had an injury to my back.

81
00:59:37.754 --> 00:59:41.754
And then if you lie down like that, you have that pain here.

82
00:59:41.754 --> 00:59:43.754
Then you can still rest a bit and hopefully then you go to visit.

83
00:59:43.754 --> 00:59:46.754
But with a toothache, there is no escaping it.

84
00:59:46.754 --> 00:59:50.754
Then you really are lying there standing.

85
00:59:50.754 --> 00:59:54.754
Really, that was not normal.

86
00:59:54.754 --> 01:00:00.754
But fortunately, after a lot of astronaut food, it has now gone down a bit.

87
01:00:04.754 --> 01:00:10.754
But God has placed amazing things in us that we also have healing effects in our bodies.

88
01:00:10.754 --> 01:00:14.754
The human body is made by God.

89
01:00:14.754 --> 01:00:16.754
Amazing. Really amazing.

90
01:00:16.754 --> 01:00:20.754
But by Thursday, Vanessa asked, honey, are you going to break?

91
01:00:20.754 --> 01:00:23.754
The way you look now, I didn't think so.

92
01:00:23.754 --> 01:00:27.754
And I said, no yes, I want to do Philippians 4. I want to break.

93
01:00:27.754 --> 01:00:29.754
Yes, hallelujah, praise the Lord.

94
01:00:29.754 --> 01:00:34.754
If pain were a number, then last Thursday it was a 9 or a 10.

95
01:00:34.754 --> 01:00:38.754
And now I'm at a 1, 2. It's still a bit annoying.

96
01:00:38.754 --> 01:00:41.754
But well, it will be fine.

97
01:00:41.754 --> 01:00:45.754
Philippians chapter 4. Really an amazing chapter.

98
01:00:45.754 --> 01:00:48.754
And I want to go through this together.

99
01:00:48.754 --> 01:00:52.754
There are two profound mysteries in this chapter.

100
01:00:52.754 --> 01:00:57.754
And I just really think it's super cool to be able to read this together.

101
01:00:57.754 --> 01:01:00.754
Do you have your Bible with you?

102
01:01:00.754 --> 01:01:03.754
And are you at Philippians chapter 4?

103
01:01:03.754 --> 01:01:05.754
Please bring your own Bible with you.

104
01:01:05.754 --> 01:01:10.754
Let us form a church culture where we bring our own Bibles.

105
01:01:10.754 --> 01:01:14.754
You might think, why should I do that? It's also on the screen.

106
01:01:14.754 --> 01:01:17.754
It is one of the exercises that you do.

107
01:01:17.754 --> 01:01:21.754
And it is another step towards owning the Bible.

108
01:01:21.754 --> 01:01:23.754
Knowing how your sword works.

109
01:01:23.754 --> 01:01:26.754
Knowing how to handle God's Word.

110
01:01:26.754 --> 01:01:31.754
So these are all tricks to be able to form a culture together. Amen?

111
01:01:31.754 --> 01:01:34.754
Okay, here we go. Philippians chapter 4, verse 1.

112
01:01:34.754 --> 01:01:37.754
Therefore, dear brothers and sisters, make sure.

113
01:01:37.754 --> 01:01:40.754
Paul says here dear brothers and sisters.

114
01:01:40.754 --> 01:01:43.754
That you are one, what does the word say?

115
01:01:43.754 --> 01:01:47.754
Does it say become one or remain one? What does it say?

116
01:01:47.754 --> 01:01:50.754
Remain one with the Lord.

117
01:01:50.754 --> 01:01:53.754
In other words, the church in Philippi is one.

118
01:01:53.754 --> 01:01:58.754
And what it also says is that Paul says dear brothers and sisters.

119
01:01:58.754 --> 01:02:04.754
And just during the worship, I was crying and the tears were falling down my cheeks.

120
01:02:04.754 --> 01:02:08.754
Because I felt such love for this church.

121
01:02:08.754 --> 01:02:11.754
This church is doing so well.

122
01:02:11.754 --> 01:02:16.754
And I say this not to boast, but you are dear brothers and sisters.

123
01:02:16.754 --> 01:02:18.754
I love you guys.

124
01:02:18.754 --> 01:02:21.754
If we could do a group hug, maybe we should organize that someday.

125
01:02:21.754 --> 01:02:23.754
A group hug.

126
01:02:23.754 --> 01:02:25.754
Really, I would like to give everyone a hug.

127
01:02:25.754 --> 01:02:28.754
As I look around the room, you are all amazing.

128
01:02:28.754 --> 01:02:30.754
And I say this not to flatter you all.

129
01:02:30.754 --> 01:02:34.754
But when I see how your lives are growing.

130
01:02:34.754 --> 01:02:36.754
And I mean that seriously.

131
01:02:36.754 --> 01:02:38.754
And I have to be careful not to start crying again.

132
01:02:38.754 --> 01:02:41.754
But your lives are growing in Christ Jesus.

133
01:02:41.754 --> 01:02:45.754
And I can just say, I am proud of you, I am proud of you.

134
01:02:45.754 --> 01:02:50.754
I could mention everyone, but if I start naming names and specific names.

135
01:02:50.754 --> 01:02:53.754
Really, I am so proud of you all.

136
01:02:53.754 --> 01:02:56.754
And I see that Open Church is also one.

137
01:02:56.754 --> 01:02:58.754
We are united with each other.

138
01:02:58.754 --> 01:03:00.754
We are all looking to King Jesus. Amen.

139
01:03:00.754 --> 01:03:03.754
You should not look at me, that is not special. You should look to Jesus.

140
01:03:03.754 --> 01:03:06.754
And we are united as a church.

141
01:03:06.754 --> 01:03:11.754
And I can say this with certainty, for I see that there is healthy growth in Open Church.

142
01:03:11.754 --> 01:03:16.754
And I'm not just talking about numbers, but I'm talking about growth in Christ.

143
01:03:16.754 --> 01:03:20.754
There is worship, I see men with uplifted hands glorifying the Lord.

144
01:03:20.754 --> 01:03:23.754
There is growth in Open Church, there is unity in Open Church.

145
01:03:23.754 --> 01:03:25.754
You are dear brothers and sisters.

146
01:03:25.754 --> 01:03:28.754
I will mention names. Martijn, I am so proud of you.

147
01:03:37.754 --> 01:03:39.754
But it is just wonderful.

148
01:03:49.754 --> 01:03:53.754
And so, we must guard this together.

149
01:03:53.754 --> 01:03:55.754
We must guard this together.

150
01:03:55.754 --> 01:04:00.754
Paul says, make sure that you remain one.

151
01:04:00.754 --> 01:04:05.754
And believe me, I have been around in the churches for a while.

152
01:04:05.754 --> 01:04:09.754
And I have seen churches come and I have seen churches go.

153
01:04:09.754 --> 01:04:14.754
Vanessa and I have been part of an amazing church.

154
01:04:14.754 --> 01:04:17.754
And that church has crumbled.

155
01:04:17.754 --> 01:04:27.754
And therefore, it still exists, but it's done due to things going wrong.

156
01:04:27.754 --> 01:04:30.754
It's done due to things going wrong.

157
01:04:30.754 --> 01:04:36.754
So what Paul is saying here in that first verse, remain one with each other.

158
01:04:36.754 --> 01:04:38.754
Remain one.

159
01:04:38.754 --> 01:04:42.754
And remaining one takes effort.

160
01:04:42.754 --> 01:04:46.754
And you must invest that effort, you must give it.

161
01:04:46.754 --> 01:04:49.754
Chapter 4 is about giving.

162
01:04:49.754 --> 01:04:53.754
This chapter is about giving yourself, doing your best.

163
01:04:53.754 --> 01:04:57.754
And Paul says here, please remain one.

164
01:04:57.754 --> 01:05:01.754
Because what we have together now is amazing.

165
01:05:01.754 --> 01:05:06.754
There is growth, there is worship, there is gratitude.

166
01:05:06.754 --> 01:05:08.754
I see men growing.

167
01:05:08.754 --> 01:05:11.754
So I wanted to finish my sentence, because I was standing here crying.

168
01:05:11.754 --> 01:05:15.754
Martijn, boy, I am so proud of you, that you...

169
01:05:15.754 --> 01:05:18.754
And of course, I don't need to broadcast your entire private life.

170
01:05:18.754 --> 01:05:20.754
But you have come a long way.

171
01:05:20.754 --> 01:05:22.754
And now you are a man of God, you are simply a man of God.

172
01:05:22.754 --> 01:05:27.754
And what I will say, because I dare to say this about myself too.

173
01:05:27.754 --> 01:05:35.754
Just, your commitment to zero tolerance regarding substance abuse and alcohol and so on.

174
01:05:35.754 --> 01:05:37.754
I do that too, zero.

175
01:05:37.754 --> 01:05:39.754
And you have been doing that for a few years now.

176
01:05:39.754 --> 01:05:43.754
And I remember, a few years ago, Joël, your son, said...

177
01:05:43.754 --> 01:05:45.754
He has become a different guy.

178
01:05:45.754 --> 01:05:47.754
You have simply become a different guy.

179
01:05:47.754 --> 01:05:49.754
And I recommend this to everyone.

180
01:05:49.754 --> 01:05:52.754
Especially men, stay away from that alcohol.

181
01:05:52.754 --> 01:05:56.754
If it changes you even just a little bit throughout the week.

182
01:05:56.754 --> 01:06:00.754
If you can handle having a beer occasionally, be my guest.

183
01:06:00.754 --> 01:06:02.754
Enjoy it.

184
01:06:02.754 --> 01:06:08.754
But if you need that beer to feel a little bit intoxicated every weekend.

185
01:06:08.754 --> 01:06:10.754
To relax.

186
01:06:10.754 --> 01:06:12.754
That relaxation is not the after-effect.

187
01:06:12.754 --> 01:06:15.754
The after-effect is that you start to lower your standards.

188
01:06:15.754 --> 01:06:18.754
Then you start to take things less seriously.

189
01:06:18.754 --> 01:06:21.754
It is my call to the church.

190
01:06:21.754 --> 01:06:24.754
If alcohol is a little thing, a little thing.

191
01:06:24.754 --> 01:06:26.754
Just try it.

192
01:06:26.754 --> 01:06:29.754
Just like God often says, just try, test me once.

193
01:06:29.754 --> 01:06:32.754
Just try it. Go a year without alcohol.

194
01:06:32.754 --> 01:06:34.754
You can see, are you going that way.

195
01:06:34.754 --> 01:06:36.754
God is so amazing.

196
01:06:36.754 --> 01:06:39.754
And just as Martijn is a man of God, there is Willem.

197
01:06:39.754 --> 01:06:41.754
You are a man of God, boy, really.

198
01:06:41.754 --> 01:06:43.754
A fantastic guy.

199
01:06:43.754 --> 01:06:44.754
Just a man of God.

200
01:06:44.754 --> 01:06:46.754
And Tjolda, you are lucky with that guy.

201
01:06:46.754 --> 01:06:49.754
And first you were married to a baptismal head.

202
01:06:49.754 --> 01:06:51.754
And now you are married to a man of God.

203
01:06:51.754 --> 01:06:53.754
And that is so cool.

204
01:06:53.754 --> 01:06:57.754
And it is so beautiful to see a family thrive so powerfully.

205
01:06:57.754 --> 01:07:00.754
That is bam, that is so cool.

206
01:07:00.754 --> 01:07:05.754
And it is so beautiful to see a family come to bloom in that unity.

207
01:07:05.754 --> 01:07:07.754
And to see it come in health.

208
01:07:07.754 --> 01:07:12.754
For us fathers, we can build families.

209
01:07:12.754 --> 01:07:16.754
But we can also destructively tear families apart.

210
01:07:16.754 --> 01:07:19.754
That is what we men have received from God.

211
01:07:19.754 --> 01:07:22.754
We are leaders by nature.

212
01:07:22.754 --> 01:07:27.754
God has positioned us as priests and as leaders over our families.

213
01:07:27.754 --> 01:07:31.754
We can bring our families under the cross in Christ.

214
01:07:31.754 --> 01:07:33.754
And that is a powerful source.

215
01:07:33.754 --> 01:07:38.754
But with that same power, we can destroy families with everything we have.

216
01:07:38.754 --> 01:07:41.754
I would say, men, go that way together with Jesus.

217
01:07:41.754 --> 01:07:43.754
Amen.

218
01:07:45.754 --> 01:07:46.754
Hallelujah.

219
01:07:46.754 --> 01:07:52.754
Therefore, dear brothers and sisters, make sure that you remain one with the Lord Jesus.

220
01:07:52.754 --> 01:07:56.754
Paul is so in love with the church in Philippi.

221
01:07:56.754 --> 01:07:59.754
Haha, funny name, Philippi.

222
01:07:59.754 --> 01:08:01.754
Lommel is also a funny name.

223
01:08:01.754 --> 01:08:04.754
But he is so happy with this church.

224
01:08:04.754 --> 01:08:07.754
And you can see that continuously reflected in this letter.

225
01:08:07.754 --> 01:08:10.754
That he rewards them with all kinds of lovely things.

226
01:08:10.754 --> 01:08:12.754
He calls them dear brothers and sisters.

227
01:08:12.754 --> 01:08:18.754
Dear brothers and sisters of Open Church, let us love one another in this church.

228
01:08:18.754 --> 01:08:21.754
Just call each other brother and sister.

229
01:08:21.754 --> 01:08:22.754
Be good to one another.

230
01:08:22.754 --> 01:08:23.754
Call each other friend.

231
01:08:23.754 --> 01:08:24.754
Call each other girlfriend.

232
01:08:24.754 --> 01:08:26.754
Be good to one another.

233
01:08:26.754 --> 01:08:27.754
Love one another.

234
01:08:27.754 --> 01:08:34.754
This church, the church of Jesus Christ, is a training ground for the kingdom of God.

235
01:08:34.754 --> 01:08:38.754
We still have to do this together for a long time.

236
01:08:38.754 --> 01:08:45.754
And this church is a place, a workshop where we can practice loving one another together.

237
01:08:45.754 --> 01:08:50.754
And here, with everything we have around us in this world, we are being pulled.

238
01:08:50.754 --> 01:08:54.754
And that is why Paul also says, make sure that you remain one with each other.

239
01:08:54.754 --> 01:08:58.754
There are always reasons to pull each other apart and this and that.

240
01:08:58.754 --> 01:09:02.754
But that is why it is an exercise for us in the here and now.

241
01:09:02.754 --> 01:09:07.754
To remain one and to commit to that in Jesus' mighty name.

242
01:09:07.754 --> 01:09:11.754
And Paul says then, as we continue, I love you all.

243
01:09:11.754 --> 01:09:13.754
I love you all, he says.

244
01:09:13.754 --> 01:09:16.754
I long to see you again.

245
01:09:16.754 --> 01:09:21.754
When I was in that dentist's chair on Thursday, it echoed against the wall.

246
01:09:21.754 --> 01:09:23.754
I was going completely crazy from the pain.

247
01:09:23.754 --> 01:09:28.754
And then there's this thought in my head, maybe I can't go to church on Sunday.

248
01:09:28.754 --> 01:09:30.754
I can't possibly be in church.

249
01:09:30.754 --> 01:09:31.754
Completely throbbing, completely painful.

250
01:09:31.754 --> 01:09:34.754
Needle out of my cheek, super sad.

251
01:09:35.754 --> 01:09:39.754
And then I think to myself, maybe I can't go to church on Sunday.

252
01:09:39.754 --> 01:09:42.754
But I long to go to church.

253
01:09:42.754 --> 01:09:45.754
I want to be here. This is my go-to club.

254
01:09:45.754 --> 01:09:48.754
I want to be here. This is my place.

255
01:09:48.754 --> 01:09:51.754
For I long to see you again.

256
01:09:51.754 --> 01:09:58.754
And it is just as wonderful to meet God, but also to meet the believers.

257
01:09:58.754 --> 01:10:01.754
For in your faces, I can recognize Christ.

258
01:10:01.754 --> 01:10:05.754
And that is why it is just as wonderful to love him and to love them.

259
01:10:05.754 --> 01:10:07.754
Vertical and horizontal.

260
01:10:07.754 --> 01:10:12.754
For you must love God with all that is within you, and your neighbor as yourself.

261
01:10:12.754 --> 01:10:15.754
And all the believers. You are lovable.

262
01:10:15.754 --> 01:10:18.754
I long to see you again.

263
01:10:18.754 --> 01:10:21.754
And I am glad about you and proud of you.

264
01:10:21.754 --> 01:10:24.754
Is this not a great letter or what?

265
01:10:24.754 --> 01:10:26.754
Paul is so happy.

266
01:10:26.754 --> 01:10:28.754
And now comes verse 2.

267
01:10:28.754 --> 01:10:33.754
And that is one of the two lessons I want to teach from this last chapter.

268
01:10:33.754 --> 01:10:35.754
Then comes verse 2.

269
01:10:35.754 --> 01:10:45.754
To Iodia and to Syntyche I say that they must stop arguing and that they should be one in the Lord.

270
01:10:45.754 --> 01:10:47.754
Right?

271
01:10:47.754 --> 01:10:49.754
And...

272
01:10:49.754 --> 01:10:50.754
Wait, wait.

273
01:10:50.754 --> 01:10:52.754
And what is written here is...

274
01:10:52.754 --> 01:10:54.754
We need to pause here.

275
01:10:54.754 --> 01:10:56.754
We are going to philosophize about this for a moment.

276
01:10:59.754 --> 01:11:02.754
So we are dealing with a well-functioning church here.

277
01:11:02.754 --> 01:11:06.754
We are dealing with the church in Philippi, which is doing well.

278
01:11:06.754 --> 01:11:08.754
Paul is happy with that church.

279
01:11:08.754 --> 01:11:10.754
The people love each other.

280
01:11:10.754 --> 01:11:11.754
He is proud of them.

281
01:11:11.754 --> 01:11:12.754
He says I love you all.

282
01:11:12.754 --> 01:11:13.754
It's all good.

283
01:11:13.754 --> 01:11:14.754
You are doing well.

284
01:11:14.754 --> 01:11:15.754
Good, good, good.

285
01:11:15.754 --> 01:11:16.754
And then suddenly comes.

286
01:11:16.754 --> 01:11:20.754
Hey, tell these two women to stop arguing.

287
01:11:20.754 --> 01:11:27.754
What I want to show from that, church, is that you don't have to expect everything to be perfect in a church...

288
01:11:27.754 --> 01:11:31.754
...to be able to conclude that this church is still very healthy and good.

289
01:11:31.754 --> 01:11:33.754
Do you understand what I mean?

290
01:11:33.754 --> 01:11:36.754
So Paul says this church is good.

291
01:11:36.754 --> 01:11:37.754
It is a good church.

292
01:11:37.754 --> 01:11:38.754
I am proud of you.

293
01:11:38.754 --> 01:11:40.754
You are of one mind with each other.

294
01:11:40.754 --> 01:11:41.754
I love you guys.

295
01:11:41.754 --> 01:11:42.754
I long for you.

296
01:11:42.754 --> 01:11:43.754
I am proud of you.

297
01:11:43.754 --> 01:11:44.754
I love you.

298
01:11:44.754 --> 01:11:46.754
You are dear brothers and sisters.

299
01:11:46.754 --> 01:11:49.754
And these two women need to stop arguing with each other.

300
01:11:49.754 --> 01:11:51.754
But that's not a problem.

301
01:11:51.754 --> 01:11:53.754
And do you know what I want to say about that, church?

302
01:11:53.754 --> 01:11:57.754
If you see small fires in an open church, that's not a problem.

303
01:11:57.754 --> 01:11:59.754
We're working on it.

304
01:11:59.754 --> 01:12:04.754
And people should just love each other in love in the Holy Spirit.

305
01:12:04.754 --> 01:12:08.754
One might say something to the other that the other might receive.

306
01:12:08.754 --> 01:12:10.754
If they then think, wow, I don't like that you say it like that.

307
01:12:10.754 --> 01:12:11.754
Doesn't matter.

308
01:12:11.754 --> 01:12:13.754
Love one another.

309
01:12:13.754 --> 01:12:15.754
Just get over it.

310
01:12:15.754 --> 01:12:18.754
Just leave it at the cross of King Jesus.

311
01:12:18.754 --> 01:12:23.754
You know, if you go looking for a perfect church, you can search for a long time.

312
01:12:23.754 --> 01:12:27.754
There is no perfect church in the whole world.

313
01:12:27.754 --> 01:12:32.754
Because all those churches are filled with people like you and me.

314
01:12:32.754 --> 01:12:39.754
And if you think, I'm going to move to another church, then you are there in that other church.

315
01:12:39.754 --> 01:12:41.754
And maybe that other church was perfect at first.

316
01:12:41.754 --> 01:12:45.754
If you then go from this church to that church, that church is no longer perfect.

317
01:12:45.754 --> 01:12:48.754
Then we're in nonsense in another church.

318
01:12:48.754 --> 01:12:50.754
It makes no sense.

319
01:12:50.754 --> 01:12:52.754
It makes no sense.

320
01:12:52.754 --> 01:12:54.754
It's always people are people.

321
01:12:54.754 --> 01:13:00.754
And people always have opinions and things clash and so on.

322
01:13:00.754 --> 01:13:07.754
And that is why I find it so cool, wonderful that this sentence is in there.

323
01:13:07.754 --> 01:13:11.754
So that we can look at this sentence 2000 years later.

324
01:13:11.754 --> 01:13:18.754
And Paul says about this church, about the Philippian church, that it is a perfect church in his eyes.

325
01:13:18.754 --> 01:13:22.754
They are one. I am proud of you. I long for you.

326
01:13:22.754 --> 01:13:25.754
You are doing well. Your faith is good.

327
01:13:25.754 --> 01:13:27.754
Everything is great. A solid ten.

328
01:13:27.754 --> 01:13:29.754
Yes, things do happen sometimes.

329
01:13:29.754 --> 01:13:33.754
These two women are arguing with each other, as women can argue.

330
01:13:33.754 --> 01:13:37.754
And Paul says, just stop that.

331
01:13:37.754 --> 01:13:39.754
Just stop it.

332
01:13:39.754 --> 01:13:46.754
And so if you are in the church and you see things that could have been better.

333
01:13:46.754 --> 01:13:49.754
Pray for the church.

334
01:13:49.754 --> 01:13:55.754
If you are in this church and you think, yes, but yes, this church is like this.

335
01:13:55.754 --> 01:13:58.754
Yes, I think so. I know.

336
01:13:58.754 --> 01:14:02.754
There are still a billion things we can do.

337
01:14:03.754 --> 01:14:11.754
Also, I know that Open Church does not do all the things that are possible in the world.

338
01:14:11.754 --> 01:14:15.754
There are still so many ministries that we could add.

339
01:14:15.754 --> 01:14:20.754
When I drive from here to Hasselt, I see at least twenty brothels.

340
01:14:20.754 --> 01:14:23.754
Don't you think God's heart weeps over that?

341
01:14:23.754 --> 01:14:26.754
That we need to tackle prostitution in this area?

342
01:14:26.754 --> 01:14:28.754
But you shouldn't do it yourself.

343
01:14:28.754 --> 01:14:32.754
You should do it when God's power comes upon you and calls you to do it.

344
01:14:32.754 --> 01:14:37.754
If people do that prematurely, then you will face a power imbalance.

345
01:14:37.754 --> 01:14:40.754
And then you will get hard blows from the kingdom of darkness.

346
01:14:40.754 --> 01:14:44.754
For even though it is a fallen kingdom.

347
01:14:44.754 --> 01:14:48.754
You must be called with a certain allowance of power and grace.

348
01:14:48.754 --> 01:14:52.754
And protection from the Holy Spirit before you tackle anything.

349
01:14:52.754 --> 01:14:57.754
You shouldn't just fly to India or Thailand to tackle the heaviest issues.

350
01:14:57.754 --> 01:15:00.754
And just think, then I will tackle it.

351
01:15:00.754 --> 01:15:02.754
Who do you think you are?

352
01:15:02.754 --> 01:15:06.754
But you must do things in the way that God says you should do them.

353
01:15:06.754 --> 01:15:08.754
When God says that you should do it.

354
01:15:08.754 --> 01:15:11.754
And in the way that God says you should do it.

355
01:15:11.754 --> 01:15:17.754
And so Open Church does what we now believe we must do.

356
01:15:17.754 --> 01:15:21.754
And maybe we have it a percentage wrong.

357
01:15:21.754 --> 01:15:24.754
Maybe we had, or should have.

358
01:15:24.754 --> 01:15:26.754
But we are doing our best.

359
01:15:26.754 --> 01:15:29.754
And so if you are here in Open Church.

360
01:15:29.754 --> 01:15:31.754
And you are in Open Church.

361
01:15:31.754 --> 01:15:34.754
And at first it's all glory and nice to sing together.

362
01:15:34.754 --> 01:15:35.754
And this and that.

363
01:15:35.754 --> 01:15:39.754
But at a certain point when you see that you're starting to get frustrated.

364
01:15:39.754 --> 01:15:41.754
Yes, but well.

365
01:15:41.754 --> 01:15:44.754
And I think this, just stop it says Paul.

366
01:15:44.754 --> 01:15:46.754
Just stop it.

367
01:15:47.754 --> 01:15:50.754
Take that joy back.

368
01:15:50.754 --> 01:15:52.754
Pursue joy.

369
01:15:52.754 --> 01:15:54.754
Pursue gratitude.

370
01:15:54.754 --> 01:15:57.754
If you pursue gratitude.

371
01:15:57.754 --> 01:15:59.754
Then you cannot complain.

372
01:15:59.754 --> 01:16:02.754
If you have a smile on your face.

373
01:16:02.754 --> 01:16:04.754
Then you cannot complain.

374
01:16:04.754 --> 01:16:07.754
I say this more often in Open Church.

375
01:16:07.754 --> 01:16:09.754
I can see it so clearly in people.

376
01:16:09.754 --> 01:16:12.754
Because you all look at me.

377
01:16:12.754 --> 01:16:15.754
I look at all of you by myself.

378
01:16:15.754 --> 01:16:18.754
And that is the calling I have received.

379
01:16:18.754 --> 01:16:20.754
And I can, and I mean this seriously.

380
01:16:20.754 --> 01:16:22.754
Vanessa and I also experience this regularly.

381
01:16:22.754 --> 01:16:24.754
I can see it just by looking at the whole crowd.

382
01:16:24.754 --> 01:16:27.754
I can tell if someone carries joy or does not carry joy.

383
01:16:27.754 --> 01:16:29.754
Right?

384
01:16:29.754 --> 01:16:30.754
But I mean that seriously.

385
01:16:30.754 --> 01:16:33.754
I can see from someone's face that there was once joy.

386
01:16:33.754 --> 01:16:35.754
And suddenly that face becomes gray again.

387
01:16:35.754 --> 01:16:38.754
And then I say, what's up with this guy?

388
01:16:38.754 --> 01:16:40.754
What's up with that guy?

389
01:16:40.754 --> 01:16:41.754
I can see it just like that.

390
01:16:41.754 --> 01:16:42.754
Do you know why?

391
01:16:42.754 --> 01:16:44.754
It's very simple.

392
01:16:44.754 --> 01:16:45.754
It's life.

393
01:16:45.754 --> 01:16:47.754
It's death.

394
01:16:47.754 --> 01:16:48.754
It's light.

395
01:16:48.754 --> 01:16:49.754
Or it's dark.

396
01:16:49.754 --> 01:16:50.754
It's happy.

397
01:16:50.754 --> 01:16:51.754
Or it's not happy.

398
01:16:51.754 --> 01:16:53.754
It's grateful.

399
01:16:53.754 --> 01:16:55.754
Or it's not grateful.

400
01:16:55.754 --> 01:16:57.754
There is no middle ground.

401
01:16:57.754 --> 01:16:59.754
It's just not there.

402
01:16:59.754 --> 01:17:02.754
And so you have to choose for yourself, you know.

403
01:17:02.754 --> 01:17:08.754
If over the past ten years Vanessa and I have been able to do this work.

404
01:17:08.754 --> 01:17:11.754
If all the people had stayed in Opelkerk.

405
01:17:11.754 --> 01:17:13.754
With a sense of gratitude.

406
01:17:13.754 --> 01:17:15.754
With a thankfulness.

407
01:17:15.754 --> 01:17:19.754
If they had stayed, then this building would have been built five times more.

408
01:17:19.754 --> 01:17:21.754
And I will go even further back.

409
01:17:21.754 --> 01:17:24.754
If the people had stayed in Reelbot.

410
01:17:24.754 --> 01:17:27.754
From the day my parents founded this church.

411
01:17:27.754 --> 01:17:30.754
Then the entire PSV stadium would have been filled.

412
01:17:30.754 --> 01:17:32.754
And I mean that seriously.

413
01:17:32.754 --> 01:17:34.754
And that has to do with just one thing.

414
01:17:34.754 --> 01:17:36.754
Unity.

415
01:17:36.754 --> 01:17:38.754
It has to do with just one thing.

416
01:17:38.754 --> 01:17:40.754
And that is unity.

417
01:17:40.754 --> 01:17:43.754
You just have to be one with each other.

418
01:17:43.754 --> 01:17:44.754
We have but one Lord.

419
01:17:44.754 --> 01:17:46.754
We have but one King.

420
01:17:46.754 --> 01:17:48.754
We have but one Spirit.

421
01:17:48.754 --> 01:17:52.754
And we must together share that same Holy Spirit.

422
01:17:52.754 --> 01:17:55.754
So you cannot be divided from each other.

423
01:17:55.754 --> 01:17:56.754
It is impossible.

424
01:17:56.754 --> 01:17:58.754
You cannot be divided from each other.

425
01:17:58.754 --> 01:18:01.754
And run off with a piece of division somewhere else.

426
01:18:01.754 --> 01:18:03.754
For I warn you here.

427
01:18:03.754 --> 01:18:05.754
If you walk around with division in your heart.

428
01:18:05.754 --> 01:18:08.754
Your whole joy will go down the drain.

429
01:18:08.754 --> 01:18:11.754
A few years ago there was someone here in Opelkerk.

430
01:18:11.754 --> 01:18:13.754
There was a group of people in Opelkerk.

431
01:18:13.754 --> 01:18:15.754
At first, they were super enthusiastic.

432
01:18:15.754 --> 01:18:17.754
Hallelujah, praise the Lord Tambourine.

433
01:18:17.754 --> 01:18:19.754
And everyone was happy.

434
01:18:19.754 --> 01:18:22.754
And after a few years or so.

435
01:18:22.754 --> 01:18:24.754
Not even that long, I think.

436
01:18:24.754 --> 01:18:26.754
You saw the joy diminish.

437
01:18:26.754 --> 01:18:29.754
And eventually, the last of that group.

438
01:18:29.754 --> 01:18:30.754
Left.

439
01:18:30.754 --> 01:18:32.754
And before that person left.

440
01:18:32.754 --> 01:18:35.754
They were actually quite amicable towards everyone.

441
01:18:35.754 --> 01:18:36.754
All behavior says to walk.

442
01:18:36.754 --> 01:18:37.754
As if it was a farewell.

443
01:18:37.754 --> 01:18:39.754
That was hypocrisy.

444
01:18:39.754 --> 01:18:42.754
And just before that person left.

445
01:18:42.754 --> 01:18:44.754
I stopped my feet just before they stumbled.

446
01:18:44.754 --> 01:18:46.754
No, I don't know that.

447
01:18:46.754 --> 01:18:48.754
But I stood up for it.

448
01:18:48.754 --> 01:18:49.754
And I said,

449
01:18:49.754 --> 01:18:50.754
What are you going to do?

450
01:18:50.754 --> 01:18:52.754
And yes, this is not good.

451
01:18:52.754 --> 01:18:53.754
And that is not good.

452
01:18:53.754 --> 01:18:54.754
And that is not good.

453
01:18:54.754 --> 01:18:55.754
And then I said.

454
01:18:55.754 --> 01:18:57.754
Yes, but wait a moment.

455
01:18:57.754 --> 01:19:00.754
When we did the new start course together.

456
01:19:00.754 --> 01:19:02.754
And when I got to baptize you.

457
01:19:02.754 --> 01:19:04.754
You were full of joy.

458
01:19:04.754 --> 01:19:07.754
You were full of joy.

459
01:19:07.754 --> 01:19:09.754
And you were happy with Jesus.

460
01:19:09.754 --> 01:19:10.754
And happy with the salvation.

461
01:19:10.754 --> 01:19:12.754
And you were happy with everything.

462
01:19:12.754 --> 01:19:13.754
I just say.

463
01:19:13.754 --> 01:19:15.754
I have been seeing you for half a year now.

464
01:19:15.754 --> 01:19:18.754
Raw, gray, and angry.

465
01:19:18.754 --> 01:19:19.754
And I said.

466
01:19:19.754 --> 01:19:20.754
And I warn you.

467
01:19:20.754 --> 01:19:22.754
If you go.

468
01:19:22.754 --> 01:19:23.754
You have to decide for yourself.

469
01:19:23.754 --> 01:19:26.754
We have no blockades at the door here.

470
01:19:26.754 --> 01:19:27.754
You have to decide for yourself.

471
01:19:27.754 --> 01:19:29.754
And I will not stop you either.

472
01:19:29.754 --> 01:19:32.754
The Father in the story of the prodigal son.

473
01:19:32.754 --> 01:19:33.754
Did not stop the son either.

474
01:19:33.754 --> 01:19:34.754
Do you understand what I mean?

475
01:19:34.754 --> 01:19:36.754
You are free to go.

476
01:19:36.754 --> 01:19:38.754
But I warn you.

477
01:19:38.754 --> 01:19:39.754
Everything is going to ruin.

478
01:19:39.754 --> 01:19:40.754
And wow.

479
01:19:40.754 --> 01:19:42.754
Before I come across as sectarian.

480
01:19:42.754 --> 01:19:44.754
It is not about this church.

481
01:19:44.754 --> 01:19:46.754
It's about joy.

482
01:19:46.754 --> 01:19:48.754
It's about gratitude.

483
01:19:48.754 --> 01:19:50.754
It's about unity.

484
01:19:50.754 --> 01:19:53.754
It's about doing our best.

485
01:19:53.754 --> 01:19:55.754
For all the little things.

486
01:19:55.754 --> 01:19:57.754
Vanessa sometimes calls them little foxes.

487
01:19:57.754 --> 01:20:00.754
Little foxes that want to steal and bite.

488
01:20:00.754 --> 01:20:03.754
Little things that can bite you.

489
01:20:03.754 --> 01:20:04.754
Disagreements.

490
01:20:04.754 --> 01:20:05.754
And yes.

491
01:20:05.754 --> 01:20:07.754
Then that was said.

492
01:20:07.754 --> 01:20:10.754
The church doesn't have to be perfect.

493
01:20:10.754 --> 01:20:11.754
Believe me.

494
01:20:11.754 --> 01:20:13.754
We will never manage that.

495
01:20:13.754 --> 01:20:17.754
This church will never manage to be perfect.

496
01:20:17.754 --> 01:20:19.754
I don't know if you can still remember it.

497
01:20:19.754 --> 01:20:20.754
But two weeks ago I stood on this podium.

498
01:20:20.754 --> 01:20:22.754
Then I said something.

499
01:20:22.754 --> 01:20:24.754
And the next day I had to rectify that.

500
01:20:24.754 --> 01:20:26.754
Did you all read it?

501
01:20:26.754 --> 01:20:28.754
So I sent a message to the church.

502
01:20:28.754 --> 01:20:29.754
To rectify something.

503
01:20:29.754 --> 01:20:30.754
I said something.

504
01:20:30.754 --> 01:20:32.754
Which I didn't mean that way.

505
01:20:32.754 --> 01:20:35.754
But it came out very awkwardly.

506
01:20:35.754 --> 01:20:37.754
Because I am already once out of line.

507
01:20:37.754 --> 01:20:40.754
And so it really came out completely wrong.

508
01:20:40.754 --> 01:20:41.754
What I said.

509
01:20:41.754 --> 01:20:43.754
And there was a bit of a wave.

510
01:20:43.754 --> 01:20:45.754
Some people thought.

511
01:20:45.754 --> 01:20:47.754
Because I always seem to be showing off.

512
01:20:47.754 --> 01:20:49.754
So some people had to laugh a bit.

513
01:20:49.754 --> 01:20:53.754
But I personally felt a sting of.

514
01:20:53.754 --> 01:20:54.754
I shouldn't have said that.

515
01:20:54.754 --> 01:20:56.754
Because it was actually about the Lord.

516
01:20:56.754 --> 01:20:58.754
And so the next day.

517
01:20:58.754 --> 01:21:00.754
I just rectified that to the church.

518
01:21:00.754 --> 01:21:01.754
I said.

519
01:21:01.754 --> 01:21:02.754
Sorry guys.

520
01:21:02.754 --> 01:21:03.754
I shouldn't have said that.

521
01:21:03.754 --> 01:21:04.754
For it was not my intention.

522
01:21:04.754 --> 01:21:06.754
To present something humorous.

523
01:21:06.754 --> 01:21:09.754
About the suffering of our Lord Jesus.

524
01:21:09.754 --> 01:21:11.754
But I wanted to nuance something.

525
01:21:11.754 --> 01:21:13.754
Because the saying I referred to.

526
01:21:13.754 --> 01:21:16.754
Was a saying that only Dutch people, I think, know.

527
01:21:16.754 --> 01:21:18.754
Let alone all those internationals.

528
01:21:18.754 --> 01:21:19.754
What is he saying now.

529
01:21:19.754 --> 01:21:21.754
And so I did that at the moment.

530
01:21:21.754 --> 01:21:23.754
But in the nanoseconds that I said it.

531
01:21:23.754 --> 01:21:24.754
I said it wrong.

532
01:21:24.754 --> 01:21:26.754
And I want to set that right.

533
01:21:26.754 --> 01:21:28.754
The point I'm making is.

534
01:21:28.754 --> 01:21:30.754
I simply make a mistake.

535
01:21:30.754 --> 01:21:32.754
Just set it right.

536
01:21:32.754 --> 01:21:34.754
What does it matter.

537
01:21:34.754 --> 01:21:35.754
So then you set it right.

538
01:21:35.754 --> 01:21:37.754
Then you say sorry.

539
01:21:37.754 --> 01:21:39.754
And if you learn that.

540
01:21:39.754 --> 01:21:42.754
If you learn that muscle in your body.

541
01:21:42.754 --> 01:21:44.754
To say sorry regularly.

542
01:21:44.754 --> 01:21:47.754
Then you find out how easy it is to say sorry.

543
01:21:47.754 --> 01:21:49.754
It is not difficult at all.

544
01:21:49.754 --> 01:21:52.754
If you are a stubborn person.

545
01:21:52.754 --> 01:21:54.754
It is very difficult to say sorry.

546
01:21:54.754 --> 01:21:56.754
But then you must lay it at the cross of Jesus.

547
01:21:56.754 --> 01:21:58.754
If Jesus had been stubborn.

548
01:21:58.754 --> 01:22:00.754
We would not be here now.

549
01:22:00.754 --> 01:22:02.754
But Jesus was not stubborn.

550
01:22:02.754 --> 01:22:05.754
And he died on a cross for mistakes he did not make.

551
01:22:05.754 --> 01:22:07.754
So my stubbornness.

552
01:22:07.754 --> 01:22:09.754
Or my difficulty in saying sorry.

553
01:22:09.754 --> 01:22:11.754
Yes, I will say sorry about that.

554
01:22:11.754 --> 01:22:13.754
Yes, I will say sorry about that.

555
01:22:13.754 --> 01:22:15.754
And in that, I can also be an example for the whole congregation.

556
01:22:15.754 --> 01:22:16.754
To simply say.

557
01:22:16.754 --> 01:22:17.754
Guys, I shouldn't have said that.

558
01:22:17.754 --> 01:22:18.754
Sorry, I regret it.

559
01:22:18.754 --> 01:22:20.754
I am just completely a flapper.

560
01:22:20.754 --> 01:22:25.754
This week I had such pain.

561
01:22:25.754 --> 01:22:27.754
That I went to the pharmacy.

562
01:22:27.754 --> 01:22:30.754
To get ibuprofen.

563
01:22:30.754 --> 01:22:33.754
And I went to that pharmacy over there.

564
01:22:33.754 --> 01:22:35.754
And I know that person quite well.

565
01:22:35.754 --> 01:22:37.754
And she's just a nice woman.

566
01:22:37.754 --> 01:22:38.754
I can just chat with her nicely.

567
01:22:38.754 --> 01:22:39.754
When I walk in there.

568
01:22:39.754 --> 01:22:41.754
And I swing that door open.

569
01:22:41.754 --> 01:22:43.754
And I say like this.

570
01:22:43.754 --> 01:22:45.754
Give me all your narcotic drugs.

571
01:22:45.754 --> 01:22:47.754
I say like this.

572
01:22:47.754 --> 01:22:48.754
And then it wasn't that woman.

573
01:22:48.754 --> 01:22:50.754
It was another one.

574
01:22:53.754 --> 01:22:54.754
Hey.

575
01:22:54.754 --> 01:22:56.754
And that girl looks at me, man.

576
01:22:58.754 --> 01:22:59.754
What.

577
01:22:59.754 --> 01:23:02.754
She presses that red button under the counter, man.

578
01:23:04.754 --> 01:23:05.754
So I thought.

579
01:23:05.754 --> 01:23:06.754
No, I don't have it after all.

580
01:23:07.754 --> 01:23:08.754
When, man.

581
01:23:08.754 --> 01:23:10.754
I can be such a fool sometimes.

582
01:23:10.754 --> 01:23:11.754
No, no, no.

583
01:23:11.754 --> 01:23:12.754
Sorry.

584
01:23:12.754 --> 01:23:13.754
It's a joke.

585
01:23:13.754 --> 01:23:14.754
It's a joke.

586
01:23:14.754 --> 01:23:15.754
I said that.

587
01:23:15.754 --> 01:23:16.754
Weirdo.

588
01:23:18.754 --> 01:23:19.754
So yes.

589
01:23:19.754 --> 01:23:21.754
You will still hear crazy things come out of my mouth regularly.

590
01:23:21.754 --> 01:23:22.754
But you know what.

591
01:23:22.754 --> 01:23:23.754
I love Jesus.

592
01:23:23.754 --> 01:23:24.754
Okay.

593
01:23:24.754 --> 01:23:26.754
But what Paul is saying here.

594
01:23:26.754 --> 01:23:27.754
And I find that so powerful.

595
01:23:27.754 --> 01:23:28.754
And so beautiful.

596
01:23:28.754 --> 01:23:31.754
And now we are going to continue reading what Paul says here.

597
01:23:33.754 --> 01:23:36.754
To these ladies, he says that they should stop arguing.

598
01:23:36.754 --> 01:23:38.754
And that they should be one in the Lord Jesus.

599
01:23:38.754 --> 01:23:39.754
Right.

600
01:23:39.754 --> 01:23:46.754
So even in a well-functioning, growing, healthy church, things happen sometimes.

601
01:23:46.754 --> 01:23:47.754
That is not a problem.

602
01:23:47.754 --> 01:23:49.754
For here comes the point.

603
01:23:49.754 --> 01:23:51.754
For that does not mean the whole church is bad.

604
01:23:51.754 --> 01:23:53.754
For verse 3 is indeed there.

605
01:23:53.754 --> 01:23:57.754
And to you, my faithful co-worker, I ask to help these two women.

606
01:23:57.754 --> 01:23:58.754
So that is what the church is for.

607
01:23:58.754 --> 01:24:02.754
Let us also be able to sharpen each other.

608
01:24:03.754 --> 01:24:06.754
Iron sharpens iron, we say in English.

609
01:24:06.754 --> 01:24:08.754
Iron sharpens iron.

610
01:24:08.754 --> 01:24:09.754
So you need to let yourself be helped.

611
01:24:09.754 --> 01:24:13.754
For they have worked hard with me to bring the good news.

612
01:24:13.754 --> 01:24:17.754
Together with Clement and my other co-workers.

613
01:24:17.754 --> 01:24:19.754
Their names, it says.

614
01:24:19.754 --> 01:24:22.754
Their names are all in the book of life.

615
01:24:22.754 --> 01:24:23.754
Do you see this?

616
01:24:23.754 --> 01:24:26.754
So these are just good people.

617
01:24:26.754 --> 01:24:29.754
These are believers in Jesus Christ who also sometimes make a mistake.

618
01:24:29.754 --> 01:24:30.754
So what?

619
01:24:30.754 --> 01:24:32.754
Do you understand what I mean?

620
01:24:32.754 --> 01:24:36.754
And with this grace, we must understand ourselves.

621
01:24:36.754 --> 01:24:38.754
That we are not perfect.

622
01:24:38.754 --> 01:24:41.754
And you must understand that other people are not perfect.

623
01:24:41.754 --> 01:24:45.754
And if we can exchange the grace of Christ with each other in that.

624
01:24:45.754 --> 01:24:47.754
We remain one with each other.

625
01:24:47.754 --> 01:24:49.754
Do you understand what I mean?

626
01:24:49.754 --> 01:24:50.754
Praise the Lord.

627
01:24:50.754 --> 01:24:51.754
I am very happy about this.

628
01:24:51.754 --> 01:24:52.754
Verse 4.

629
01:24:52.754 --> 01:24:56.754
Always be joyful in the Lord.

630
01:24:56.754 --> 01:24:58.754
Always be joyful.

631
01:24:58.754 --> 01:25:00.754
I say it again.

632
01:25:00.754 --> 01:25:02.754
I already did this in the previous sermon.

633
01:25:02.754 --> 01:25:04.754
So Paul puts it in this Philippians sermon.

634
01:25:04.754 --> 01:25:07.754
A number of times he simply says.

635
01:25:07.754 --> 01:25:08.754
Be joyful.

636
01:25:08.754 --> 01:25:09.754
I say it again.

637
01:25:09.754 --> 01:25:11.754
Be joyful.

638
01:25:11.754 --> 01:25:14.754
Because joy, dear people,

639
01:25:14.754 --> 01:25:18.754
Ensures that you continue to grow in your love.

640
01:25:18.754 --> 01:25:21.754
And in your joy in Jesus Christ.

641
01:25:21.754 --> 01:25:24.754
If you are happy, that is.

642
01:25:24.754 --> 01:25:28.754
And you choose to be happy.

643
01:25:29.754 --> 01:25:32.754
Because happiness is a choice.

644
01:25:32.754 --> 01:25:35.754
Because when Paul says to the church.

645
01:25:35.754 --> 01:25:36.754
Be happy.

646
01:25:36.754 --> 01:25:39.754
Then happiness is a command.

647
01:25:39.754 --> 01:25:40.754
In other words.

648
01:25:40.754 --> 01:25:42.754
Happiness is a verb.

649
01:25:42.754 --> 01:25:43.754
Instead of an emotion.

650
01:25:43.754 --> 01:25:47.754
That happens to you by chance or not.

651
01:25:47.754 --> 01:25:48.754
Do you understand what I mean?

652
01:25:48.754 --> 01:25:50.754
If I say to someone.

653
01:25:50.754 --> 01:25:51.754
Go walk.

654
01:25:51.754 --> 01:25:53.754
Then that is a command to go walk.

655
01:25:53.754 --> 01:25:55.754
So if I say to someone.

656
01:25:55.754 --> 01:25:56.754
Be happy.

657
01:25:56.754 --> 01:25:58.754
Then that is a command to be happy.

658
01:25:58.754 --> 01:26:01.754
So you have no reason.

659
01:26:01.754 --> 01:26:02.754
In life.

660
01:26:02.754 --> 01:26:04.754
Not to be happy.

661
01:26:04.754 --> 01:26:07.754
You always have a reason to be happy.

662
01:26:07.754 --> 01:26:10.754
And that reason is that we have a risen Lord.

663
01:26:10.754 --> 01:26:12.754
His name is King Jesus.

664
01:26:12.754 --> 01:26:15.754
And everything, everything, everything.

665
01:26:15.754 --> 01:26:17.754
That lies beneath it.

666
01:26:17.754 --> 01:26:19.754
Is nothing but gratitude.

667
01:26:19.754 --> 01:26:21.754
And glory to the Lord.

668
01:26:22.754 --> 01:26:26.754
And I can boast about the fact that I am such a happy person.

669
01:26:26.754 --> 01:26:30.754
That sometimes I sit in the car crying tears of joy.

670
01:26:30.754 --> 01:26:32.754
Because I think about my daughter.

671
01:26:32.754 --> 01:26:34.754
Or because I think about my son.

672
01:26:34.754 --> 01:26:37.754
Or because I think about just the beauty of life.

673
01:26:37.754 --> 01:26:38.754
Then I mean this.

674
01:26:38.754 --> 01:26:40.754
I'm not exaggerating.

675
01:26:40.754 --> 01:26:43.754
Last week I drove home in my little Peugeot.

676
01:26:43.754 --> 01:26:45.754
And it passed the inspection.

677
01:26:45.754 --> 01:26:47.754
And I thought it wouldn't pass anymore.

678
01:26:47.754 --> 01:26:50.754
And I just drove home in my shabby little Peugeot.

679
01:26:51.754 --> 01:26:53.754
Tears of joy.

680
01:26:53.754 --> 01:26:55.754
And I just sent Vanessa a message.

681
01:26:55.754 --> 01:26:57.754
When I finally got home.

682
01:26:57.754 --> 01:26:59.754
And I said I am so happy.

683
01:26:59.754 --> 01:27:01.754
I am just crying from joy.

684
01:27:01.754 --> 01:27:04.754
Just how happy you can be in life.

685
01:27:04.754 --> 01:27:06.754
Because here is a challenge.

686
01:27:06.754 --> 01:27:12.754
If you wait until you have a better car.

687
01:27:12.754 --> 01:27:14.754
Than my rickety Peugeot.

688
01:27:14.754 --> 01:27:18.754
If that is the reason you can only be happy then.

689
01:27:18.754 --> 01:27:21.754
That is super shaky man.

690
01:27:21.754 --> 01:27:25.754
Because maybe you could have bought that better car once.

691
01:27:25.754 --> 01:27:27.754
And then what?

692
01:27:27.754 --> 01:27:32.754
Then there is someone who has a better version than the car you have.

693
01:27:32.754 --> 01:27:35.754
Bam, there goes your Joy.

694
01:27:35.754 --> 01:27:37.754
That is so fragile.

695
01:27:37.754 --> 01:27:39.754
That is such thin ice.

696
01:27:39.754 --> 01:27:42.754
To be able to be happy with the things in life.

697
01:27:42.754 --> 01:27:44.754
That is shaky.

698
01:27:44.754 --> 01:27:49.754
But what you can be very happy about, which is a solid foundation.

699
01:27:49.754 --> 01:27:51.754
Is the rock Jesus Christ.

700
01:27:51.754 --> 01:27:54.754
You can really be happy with that.

701
01:27:54.754 --> 01:27:56.754
For He is solid.

702
01:27:56.754 --> 01:27:58.754
There is no upgrade to Jesus.

703
01:27:58.754 --> 01:28:01.754
Jesus is the best of the best.

704
01:28:01.754 --> 01:28:03.754
Jesus is the full package.

705
01:28:03.754 --> 01:28:05.754
Jesus is amazing.

706
01:28:05.754 --> 01:28:08.754
Jesus is good, loving, reliable.

707
01:28:08.754 --> 01:28:10.754
He provides, He protects.

708
01:28:10.754 --> 01:28:13.754
He gives peace, He gives joy.

709
01:28:13.754 --> 01:28:15.754
He gives victory.

710
01:28:15.754 --> 01:28:19.754
He gives everything you need and much more.

711
01:28:19.754 --> 01:28:24.754
And then you can drive home from the inspection in your little car.

712
01:28:24.754 --> 01:28:29.754
That you think to yourself, thank you Jesus for everything I have.

713
01:28:29.754 --> 01:28:31.754
I am so happy.

714
01:28:31.754 --> 01:28:33.754
And so you must choose that.

715
01:28:33.754 --> 01:28:36.754
For you must choose it, verse 4.

716
01:28:36.754 --> 01:28:40.754
Rejoice always in the Lord.

717
01:28:40.754 --> 01:28:42.754
I say it again.

718
01:28:42.754 --> 01:28:43.754
Rejoice.

719
01:28:43.754 --> 01:28:46.754
Let all people see that you are kind.

720
01:28:46.754 --> 01:28:48.754
The Lord is near to you.

721
01:28:48.754 --> 01:28:51.754
Do not worry about anything.

722
01:28:51.754 --> 01:28:55.754
But tell God what you need in prayer.

723
01:28:55.754 --> 01:28:58.754
Thank Him for everything as well.

724
01:28:58.754 --> 01:29:01.754
I tell you, thank Him for everything as well.

725
01:29:01.754 --> 01:29:03.754
Just a pause.

726
01:29:03.754 --> 01:29:04.754
Do you do that too?

727
01:29:04.754 --> 01:29:06.754
And here is a question.

728
01:29:06.754 --> 01:29:08.754
Do you really do that?

729
01:29:08.754 --> 01:29:13.754
Because it is very easy to read your Bible daily.

730
01:29:13.754 --> 01:29:16.754
One verse or one chapter or one book of the Bible.

731
01:29:16.754 --> 01:29:19.754
You can decide for yourself how much you read.

732
01:29:19.754 --> 01:29:21.754
And then say a prayer like that.

733
01:29:21.754 --> 01:29:23.754
But do you thank God as well?

734
01:29:23.754 --> 01:29:25.754
Continuously for everything.

735
01:29:25.754 --> 01:29:27.754
I really mean what I am saying now.

736
01:29:27.754 --> 01:29:29.754
Just a challenge.

737
01:29:29.754 --> 01:29:32.754
Thank God for your marriage.

738
01:29:32.754 --> 01:29:34.754
Do you thank God for your children?

739
01:29:34.754 --> 01:29:37.754
Do you thank God for your job?

740
01:29:37.754 --> 01:29:39.754
Even if your job is difficult.

741
01:29:39.754 --> 01:29:43.754
Even if your job does not bring in what you would like it to bring in.

742
01:29:43.754 --> 01:29:45.754
Or would like it to bring in.

743
01:29:45.754 --> 01:29:49.754
Even if you have been struggling for a few years, despite inflation rising.

744
01:29:49.754 --> 01:29:54.754
And your employer has not coincidentally given you that index.

745
01:29:54.754 --> 01:29:57.754
And you are worried about how you will manage.

746
01:29:57.754 --> 01:30:00.754
Are you still grateful that you have work at all?

747
01:30:00.754 --> 01:30:03.754
This is really a challenge that I lay before all of us.

748
01:30:03.754 --> 01:30:06.754
Are you complaining about life or are you happy with life?

749
01:30:06.754 --> 01:30:09.754
Are you complaining about your marriage or are you happy with your marriage?

750
01:30:09.754 --> 01:30:13.754
Are you complaining about open church or are you happy with open church?

751
01:30:13.754 --> 01:30:16.754
Are you complaining about your children because they can be crazy sometimes?

752
01:30:16.754 --> 01:30:20.754
Or are you happy with your children because they can be crazy?

753
01:30:20.754 --> 01:30:22.754
Do you understand what I mean?

754
01:30:22.754 --> 01:30:25.754
And this is therefore a task that we all need.

755
01:30:25.754 --> 01:30:29.754
To be able to remain in Christ. Amen. Hallelujah.

756
01:30:29.754 --> 01:30:31.754
Verse 7.

757
01:30:31.754 --> 01:30:33.754
For if you are happy.

758
01:30:33.754 --> 01:30:34.754
Then.

759
01:30:34.754 --> 01:30:37.754
The word then is a condition.

760
01:30:37.754 --> 01:30:42.754
Then the peace of God, which we cannot possibly understand,

761
01:30:42.754 --> 01:30:46.754
protect your hearts and your minds in Jesus Christ.

762
01:30:49.754 --> 01:30:51.754
I need one more amen moment.

763
01:30:51.754 --> 01:30:54.754
Not yet, but I want to push it one more time

764
01:30:54.754 --> 01:30:57.754
before I continue with my next topic.

765
01:30:57.754 --> 01:31:02.754
So you must thank him, thank him, thank him, thank him, thank him.

766
01:31:03.754 --> 01:31:05.754
For in that gratitude.

767
01:31:05.754 --> 01:31:13.754
If you keep practicing that habit of gratitude diligently.

768
01:31:13.754 --> 01:31:16.754
Then a peace comes into you.

769
01:31:16.754 --> 01:31:18.754
And that is an effect.

770
01:31:18.754 --> 01:31:20.754
Then a peace comes into you.

771
01:31:20.754 --> 01:31:23.754
And that peace is even greater.

772
01:31:24.754 --> 01:31:31.754
Pastor Brian at Hillsong Church in Sydney once preached a whole series about momentum.

773
01:31:31.754 --> 01:31:40.754
The word momentum that he preached was like a boat, a heavy boat, starting to gain speed,

774
01:31:40.754 --> 01:31:45.754
then momentum comes in from weight and speed.

775
01:31:45.754 --> 01:31:51.754
As a long train starts to move slowly and begins to gain speed,

776
01:31:51.754 --> 01:31:57.754
eventually it becomes difficult to stop it, because there is a lot of weight and a lot of speed.

777
01:31:57.754 --> 01:32:00.754
When those two come together, you get a great momentum.

778
01:32:00.754 --> 01:32:05.754
I’ll lay it down for us Dutch speakers, so you understand the context.

779
01:32:05.754 --> 01:32:08.754
And that has become a life lesson for me.

780
01:32:08.754 --> 01:32:12.754
That I think to myself, I want to create moments in my life.

781
01:32:12.754 --> 01:32:17.754
I want to create moments where I ultimately want to stay engaged with Jesus.

782
01:32:17.754 --> 01:32:19.754
I want to stay engaged with His Word.

783
01:32:19.754 --> 01:32:22.754
I want to remain grateful. I want to remain of one mind.

784
01:32:22.754 --> 01:32:27.754
I want to continue praising God. I want to keep sowing in my life.

785
01:32:27.754 --> 01:32:30.754
